<title>UK: Russia sees higher privatisation revenues in '97.</title>
<headline>Russia sees higher privatisation revenues in '97.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Privatisation revenues should rise sharply next year, deputy finance minister Mikhail Kasyanov said on Friday.</p>
<p>Bankers attending the roadshow in London for Russia's planned Eurobond quoted him as saying that proceeds from selling off state firms in 1997 would be far in excess of this year's $1.6 billion.</p>
<p>He declined to predict a precise figure, but mentioned regional electricity companies as among those to be sold off.</p>
